# INCONSISTENCY THROUGH AN INDIVIDUAL CONTEXT. C(a) with C subseteq bottom gives
# bottom IN S(individual(a)) while leaving every CLASS context untouched.
# This is why entails-sub's first disjunct (findings.inconsistent) is NOT redundant
# with the second (bottom IN S(A)): omitting it makes an unrelated probe D subseteq E
# answer FALSE on an ontology that entails everything -- and does so precisely when
# the inconsistency came from the ABox encoding v0 exists to support.
# Expect: inconsistent = TRUE; unsatisfiable and subsumptions both EMPTY (undefined,
# not empty); every probe answers true.

@prefix :    <http://example.org/t#> .
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdf:  <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

<http://example.org/t> a owl:Ontology .
:C a owl:Class . :D a owl:Class . :E a owl:Class .
:C rdfs:subClassOf owl:Nothing .
:a a owl:NamedIndividual , :C .
